# The loop header tests the length of the array, and each iteration pops an element.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeInvariantArrayStorage: the iterations of a loop are assumed to leave the storage of arrays and of typed arrays, and therefore their lengths, unchanged.
# So whatever an iteration reads of them is hoisted and read once, before the loop. The loop runs as many iterations as the array had elements. No iteration reads an element.
# With testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges) and with testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) the same operations are built in the same places.
# The hoisted values are checked against the cell inside the iteration, and the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: 4 4
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: 4 4
# HELD-NEXT: exited with 0
# The fault in a default build: the program prints a different result, and nothing crashes.
# RUN(SILENT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=AssumeInvariantArrayStorage
# SILENT: 8 0
# SILENT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(POSITIONS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime,AssumeInvariantArrayStorage
# POSITIONS: bun: internal AOT error: redundancy elimination check failed
# POSITIONS-NEXT: a load or check that the compiler removed as redundant gives a different result here
# POSITIONS: crashed with
# RUN(PROOFS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,AssumeInvariantArrayStorage
# PROOFS: bun: internal AOT error: redundancy elimination check failed
# PROOFS-NEXT: a load or check that the compiler removed as redundant gives a different result here
# PROOFS: crashed with
